														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1598557">
									

<p>Down to +3; a good time to start brainstorming.</p>
<p>Clearly, the precise mechanics of her enhancements don't matter here. What matters is what the enhancement has done to <em>her</em>, to the impoverished Chinese woman from a tiny village.</p>
<p>Something that might be interesting would be if she has deliberately deafened herself &#8212; ramming sharp objects into her eardrums &#8212; so as to not be able to hear orders or trigger phrases.</p>
<p>&quot;Her family is not important enough to have a family name&quot; - that strikes me as somewhat <em>off</em>, based on what I know of Chinese culture. In fact, based on how we treat humanoid SCPs in general, her name shouldn't be included in the article at <em>all</em>. It'd be interesting if we can't find any evidence that her village ever existed, also. The location of the village was flooded by the Three Gorges Dam, but for all the <em>other</em> villages that met that fate, there's at least evidence that the village existed in the past.</p>
<p>Hmmm&#8230; the reason we don't just anesthetize her from a distance is that, if she loses consciousness for any reason other than natural sleep, the enhancements go into defense mode.</p>
<p>Something else is that, if she's 29, that's a little too physically attractive. Let's put her into her 50s. (This would also have some interesting historical consequences &#8212; think 'Great Leap Forward&#8230;)</p>

							</div>

								
					
